---
layout: base.njk
pageKey: care
title: "Website care plans"
permalink: care.html
description: Transparent website care from $79/mo for every Symbio-hosted website. See exactly what the monthly fee covers, what is separate, and how each plan works.
---

<section class="section section--tight has-aurora">
  <div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container container--narrow center">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Website care · disclosed before launch</span>
    <h1 class="section__title">Your build gets it live. Care keeps it live.</h1>
    <p class="section__lead">
      For every new website Symbio hosts and manages, care starts at <strong>$79/mo</strong> when
      the site launches. The one-time build and monthly care always appear as separate line items,
      so you know both numbers before approving the project.
    </p>
    <div class="care-policy" role="note">
      <span class="care-policy__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      No surprise subscription · month-to-month · self-managed handoff available
    </div>
    <div class="btn-row btn-row--center mt-6">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="#plans">Compare care plans</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="pricing.html">See build pricing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head section__head--center" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Two prices, two jobs</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">Build cost and care cost are not the same charge</h2>
      <p class="section__lead">One creates the website. The other operates it after launch.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="care-model" data-reveal>
      <article class="care-model__card">
        <span class="care-model__label">One time</span>
        <h3>Website build</h3>
        <p>Strategy, design, development, mobile polish, forms, testing, and launch.</p>
        <strong>Quoted before work begins</strong>
      </article>
      <article class="care-model__card care-model__card--active">
        <span class="care-model__label">Monthly after launch</span>
        <h3>Website care</h3>
        <p>Managed hosting, monitoring, maintenance, restore points, support, and included updates.</p>
        <strong>From $79/mo</strong>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight section--tint">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head section__head--center" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Where the fee goes</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">The work that continues after launch</h2>
      <p class="section__lead">
        The monthly fee is not payment for the same website twice. It covers the infrastructure
        and hands-on work required to keep a managed site healthy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="care-cost-grid">
      <article class="care-cost" data-reveal>
        <span class="care-cost__num">01</span>
        <h3>Hosting &amp; SSL</h3>
        <p>Your website stays published on managed infrastructure with encrypted HTTPS.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="care-cost" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        <span class="care-cost__num">02</span>
        <h3>Monitoring &amp; recovery</h3>
        <p>We watch availability and keep deployment history and restore points ready.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="care-cost" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
        <span class="care-cost__num">03</span>
        <h3>Platform maintenance</h3>
        <p>Security, dependency, compatibility, and performance maintenance as the web changes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="care-cost" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
        <span class="care-cost__num">04</span>
        <h3>Real human support</h3>
        <p>Minor content changes and troubleshooting from the same builders who know the site.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight" id="plans">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head section__head--center" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Monthly plans</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">Choose how hands-on you want us to be</h2>
      <p class="section__lead">
        Essential is the required minimum for new Symbio-managed websites. Upgrade when you want
        more edit time, reporting, and faster support.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      {% for plan in site.carePlans %}
        <article
          id="{{ plan.key }}"
          class="price{% if plan.featured %} price--popular{% endif %}"
          data-reveal
          data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index0 }}"
        >
          {% if plan.featured %}<span class="price__flag">Most popular</span>{% endif %}
          <h2 class="price__name">{{ plan.name }}</h2>
          {% if plan.key == "care-essential" %}
            <span class="price__kicker">Managed-site minimum</span>
          {% endif %}
          <p class="price__amount">{{ plan.price }} <small>{{ plan.cadence }}</small></p>
          <p class="price__desc">{{ plan.blurb }}</p>
          <ul class="price__features">
            {% for feature in plan.features %}
              <li>{{ feature }}</li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
          <div class="price__cta">
            <a
              class="btn {% if plan.featured %}btn--primary{% else %}btn--secondary{% endif %} btn--block"
              href="{{ plan.checkoutUrl if plan.checkoutUrl else site.checkout.url }}"
              {% if plan.checkoutUrl %}rel="noopener"{% endif %}
            >
              {% if plan.checkoutUrl %}Start {{ plan.name }} — {{ plan.price }}{{ plan.cadence }}{% else %}Choose {{ plan.name }}{% endif %}
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="note-card mt-7" data-reveal>
      <span class="note-card__tag">When billing starts</span>
      <p>
        Care begins when the website launches, not while we are building it. It is month-to-month.
        If you cancel, managed hosting, monitoring, maintenance, and support end after the paid
        billing period. Ask us for a separately quoted self-managed handoff before cancellation
        if you want to operate the site elsewhere.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight section--tint">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head section__head--center" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Clear boundaries</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">What care covers—and what needs a new quote</h2>
      <p class="section__lead">We ask before doing billable work outside your plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="scope-grid">
      <article class="scope-panel" data-reveal>
        <span class="scope-panel__label">Included on every plan</span>
        <ul class="scope-panel__list">
          <li>Managed hosting and SSL/TLS</li>
          <li>Availability monitoring and restore points</li>
          <li>Security, platform, and dependency maintenance</li>
          <li>The content-update allowance listed in your plan</li>
          <li>Support from the builders who know your website</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="scope-panel scope-panel--separate" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        <span class="scope-panel__label">Quoted separately—with approval first</span>
        <ul class="scope-panel__list">
          <li>New pages, major features, or redesigns</li>
          <li>Custom integrations, e-commerce, or app development</li>
          <li>Full copywriting, photo/video production, or ad campaigns</li>
          <li>Third-party subscriptions, domains, ads, or paid software</li>
          <li>Work beyond the plan's monthly update allowance</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="care-fineprint" data-reveal>
      Monthly update time resets each billing cycle and does not roll over. “Response time” means
      acknowledgment and triage—not guaranteed resolution time. Business hours are Monday–Friday,
      9am–6pm in the client's local time, excluding holidays.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head section__head--center" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Straight answers</span>
      <h2 class="section__title">The questions clients usually ask</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid--3">
      <article class="card card--static" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="card__title">Why is this monthly?</h3>
        <p class="card__text">
          Hosting, monitoring, maintenance, and support continue every month. The build fee only
          covers creating and launching the website.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--static" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        <h3 class="card__title">Can I host it myself?</h3>
        <p class="card__text">
          Yes. A self-managed handoff can be quoted separately. You take responsibility for
          hosting, security, maintenance, and future changes.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--static" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
        <h3 class="card__title">Will you charge extra without asking?</h3>
        <p class="card__text">
          No. If a request falls outside your plan, we explain the scope and price before starting
          that work.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="cta-band" data-reveal>
      <h2 class="cta-band__title">One build number. One care number. No surprise bill.</h2>
      <p class="cta-band__text">
        We show both before you approve the project, then start monthly care only when your site
        goes live.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
        <a class="btn btn--light btn--lg" href="{{ site.cta.url }}">Get my free scan</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary btn--lg" href="{{ site.checkout.url }}">Open checkout</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary btn--lg" href="pricing.html">See build pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
